Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4720555860442438, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3970882372060627, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6469794, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engi