\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:16] Evan**: Finished the parser swap the audit flagged — pulled out the problem library and dropped in a replacement. Calling that step done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:18] Diana**: Nice turnaround. I'll fold it into the re-scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:21] Charlie**: Did you check the new one's license closely, or just take the package listing at face value?\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"2536eeff413cf064\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.40946659199806434, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.29011497428294913, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6879537, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1186, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4055327146934319, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.29781617813347416, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6568713, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- **2026-09-18**: Bob - Buffer Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\\n - *Refactored the disk-usage monitor to allow a 10% buffer above quota, since the reopened hard halt was tripping too aggressively on production-like batches.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 09 18 bob buffer refactor activ reopen refactor the disk usag monitor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota sinc the reopen hard halt wa trip too aggress on product like batch\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Sto