{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"CIPH-15 Docker packaging 2026-09-22","page":2},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \" - *Task opened to design the manual-review quarantine workflow for low-confidence OCR.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - End-to-end quarantine test; 90% threshold still integrating (Active)\\n\\n - *Ran an end-to-end quarantine test exercising the UI and metadata path; confidence-threshold integration remains Active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"task open to design the manual review quarantin workflow for low confid ocr 2026 09 18 diana end to end quarantin test 90 threshold still integr activ ran an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path confid threshold integr remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"e90e536e6f3595fa\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3821878615477936, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.25702428792541954, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6742362, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"id\": \"af63545a0d15b5f6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37954235654779367, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.25702428792541954, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66541785, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 947, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:55\", \"token_count\": 416, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## What was added\\n\\nAn asynchronous scheduler that accepts batch API jobs and dispatches them to worker threads without blocking the request path, building on the multi-threading work already integrated into the batch CLI.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Design\\n\\nJobs are queued with a job ID returned immediately to the caller; a separate status endpoint reports progress. Workers pull from the same queue used by the multi-threaded batch path.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers the scheduler's implementation and design only. It does not cover any concurrency issues found during later evaluation of the scheduler under load; those are separate from what this note documents.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load what wa ad an asynchron schedul that accept batch api job and dispatch them to worker thread without block the request path build on the multi thread work alreadi integr into the batch cli sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load design job are queu with a job id return immedi to the caller a separ status endpoint report progress worker pull from the same queue use by the multi thread batch path sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load scope this note cover the schedul s implement and design onli it doe not cover ani concurr issu found dure later evalu of the schedul under load those are separ from what this note document\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e90a788a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"0081bbcc02cb4f7b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37852418954779365, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.25702428792541954, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66202396, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"docu